# Anchored (leading /) so ONLY the working files at eval/ root stay untracked — the committed,
# append-only quality record under eval/history/ must never be swallowed by these names (Phase B6:
# an untracked quality record is how a 12-day capability collapse left no versioned trace).
/scorecard.json
/sessions.json
/REPORT.md
/controls-scorecard.json
/holdout-scorecard.json
/out/
# phase.json — the SESSION-phase wall-clock window each on-box run writes for the TG-204 tier A/B
# (eval/tier-ab.sh reads it to attribute proxy telemetry). Per-run, machine-local, and regenerated every
# arm: exactly the shape the anchored names above exist for. The COMMITTED tier-ab record is the archived
# verdict under eval/history/, which the leading slashes here deliberately leave alone.
/phase.json
